  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of TB and HIV Clinical Mentoring Services in Somalia and Somaliland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In partnership with the Global Fund for AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria, the project aims to improve human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) and tuberculosis (TB) services provision in Somalia and Somaliland by setting up a clinical mentoring system to enhance clinicians&#x2019; treatment skills. Clinical mentoring will enable health professionals to practice new skills in clinical settings with the support and guidance of a more specialized and experienced clinician. Intensive, practical training is especially important in HIV care and treatment given the diversity of illnesses associated with AIDS and the complexities involved in second/third line antiretroviral therapy and treatment of multi-drug resistant TB.</narrative>
  </description>
